MEM                                                            [3.0]
---

Format:      MEM

Purpose:     Displays a compact memory mapper listing.

Use:         For every memory mapper in the system,  one   line   is
        printed with its slot and its total,  reserved (used by  the
        system or by user programs) and free memory,  in  kilobytes,
        followed by a line with the totals over all the mappers.

             Then the size of the RAM disk is printed (only when one
        exists),  followed by the end address of the TPA (the memory
        available  to  transient  programs,  which starts at address
        0100h) and the equivalent TPA size.

             The output is at most 32 characters wide,  so  that  it
        also  looks  good  in  the 32 column screen modes.  For more
        detailed information use the MEMORY command.

Examples:

        MEM
        Slot     Total Reserved     Free
        ----     ----- --------     ----
         3-2     1024K      48K     976K
           1       64K      64K       0K

        Total:   1088K     112K     976K

        RAM disk size: 128K
        TPA end address: D706h
        TPA size: 53K

             A system with a 1024K memory mapper in slot 3-2  and  a
        64K one in slot 1,  with a 128K RAM disk in use.
